=== HINT 1 ===
fprintf works like printf but takes a FILE* as first argument:
  fprintf(fw, "%d\n", i);

=== HINT 2 ===
fscanf works like scanf but reads from a file:
  fscanf(fr, "%d", &val);
It returns the number of items successfully read.

=== HINT 3 ===
Write loop:
  for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
      fprintf(fw, "%d\n", i);

=== HINT 4 (SPOILER) ===
// write section:
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
    fprintf(fw, "%d\n", i);

// read section (inside the existing for loop):
fscanf(fr, "%d", &val);
